WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.153
Our matrix has order four
u squared, with u odd.

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.620
We will relabel its cycle
using two coordinates.

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:11.180
Send position j to j modulo
four, and j modulo u squared.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.260
These are two residue dials.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:18.210
In the illustration, u equals three,
so their lengths are four and nine.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.673
Position one becomes one, one.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:27.533
Position four becomes zero, four.
Position nine becomes one, zero.

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:30.480
Each step advances both dials together.

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:33.660
Why does this lose no positions?

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:37.220
Suppose two positions have the same pair.

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:41.500
Their difference is divisible
by four and by u squared.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:46.280
These lengths are coprime, so their
difference is divisible by four u squared.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.860
They were the same position
on the original cycle. The

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:53.740
two descriptions also have the same
number of positions. In our example,

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:57.100
all thirty six positions
fill a four by nine grid,

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.700
with each cell used exactly once.

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:04.030
Addition is preserved too:
four plus nine is thirteen,

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:07.153
and their coordinate
pairs add to one, four.

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:12.300
In general, add each coordinate modulo
its own length. Thus the cyclic group

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:17.000
of order four u squared is isomorphic to
the product of these two cyclic groups.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.960
Now translate the polynomial.

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:23.940
Introduce Z for the four cycle
and P for the u squared cycle.

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:26.700
The generator X maps to Z times P.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:30.840
Therefore X to the j becomes
Z to the j times P to the j,

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:32.980
with the exponents reduced separately.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.500
Keep the same coefficient h
sub j attached throughout.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:41.940
Every sign moves to exactly one new
label; no signs are added or changed.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.540
Multiplication respects
addition of exponents.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:51.020
Inversion negates both coordinates, so
the star operation is preserved as well.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:56.100
Consequently the original norm identity
becomes h of Z, P times h star of Z,

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:00.910
P equals four u squared. The new
relations are Z to the fourth equals one,

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:05.640
and P to the u squared equals
one. We have changed coordinates,

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:09.800
while keeping the same sign
data and the same norm identity.
